## Documentation

Run `npm run docs` to generate Markdown reference docs into `docs/` (modules + models),
auto-discovered from your source. Request bodies and query params are derived from the Joi
schemas (`validateBody`/`validateQuery`), and response examples are inferred from the
controller → service → model chain — so you normally write only `// @doc <summary>` (and an
optional `// @desc`). The `@body` / `@query` / `@response` tags are overrides for cases
inference can't reach. Run `npm run docs -- --check` in CI to fail the build when docs drift.
Commit `docs/` so AI assistants and humans get an up-to-date map of the API.

