## Social Sign-In

This backend uses **ID-token verification** — the same flow for web and mobile.
Your client (web SDK or native iOS/Android/React-Native) performs the sign-in UI,
obtains a signed **ID token**, and POSTs it to the backend. The server verifies the
token against <%= socialGoogle && socialApple ? "Google's / Apple's" : (socialGoogle ? "Google's" : "Apple's") %>
public keys, then finds-or-creates the user and issues the **same session cookie**
as password login. Accounts are linked by verified email, so a user keeps one account
across password and social sign-in.

> Send requests with `credentials: 'include'` (web) so the session cookie is stored.

<% if (socialGoogle) { -%>
### Google

**Endpoint:** `POST /auth/google` — body `{ "idToken": "<google ID token>" }`

**Setup:** In [Google Cloud Console](https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials)
create an OAuth client ID for each platform you ship (Web, iOS, Android). Put every
client ID that can call this backend into `GOOGLE_CLIENT_IDS` (comma-separated) — the
token's `aud` must match one of them.

```js
// Web — Google Identity Services
google.accounts.id.initialize({
  client_id: 'YOUR_WEB_CLIENT_ID.apps.googleusercontent.com',
  callback: async ({ credential }) => {
    await fetch('/auth/google', {
      method: 'POST',
      headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
      credentials: 'include',
      body: JSON.stringify({ idToken: credential }),
    });
  },
});
```

```js
// Mobile — @react-native-google-signin/google-signin (configure with webClientId)
const { data } = await GoogleSignin.signIn();
await fetch('https://your-api/auth/google', {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
  body: JSON.stringify({ idToken: data.idToken }),
});
```

<% } -%>
<% if (socialApple) { -%>
### Apple

**Endpoint:** `POST /auth/apple` — body `{ "identityToken": "...", "nonce": "...", "name": "..." }`

**Setup:** In the [Apple Developer portal](https://developer.apple.com/account/resources/identifiers/list/serviceId)
enable Sign in with Apple. Put your **Services ID** (web) and/or app **bundle ID**
(native) into `APPLE_CLIENT_IDS` (comma-separated). Apple sends the user's **name only
on the first sign-in**, and in the client payload — not the token — so forward it.

```js
// Web — Sign in with Apple JS
const res = await AppleID.auth.signIn();
await fetch('/auth/apple', {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
  credentials: 'include',
  body: JSON.stringify({
    identityToken: res.authorization.id_token,
    name: res.user ? `${res.user.name.firstName} ${res.user.name.lastName}` : undefined,
  }),
});
```

```js
// Mobile — expo-apple-authentication
const credential = await AppleAuthentication.signInAsync({
  requestedScopes: [
    AppleAuthentication.AppleAuthenticationScope.FULL_NAME,
    AppleAuthentication.AppleAuthenticationScope.EMAIL,
  ],
});
await fetch('https://your-api/auth/apple', {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
  body: JSON.stringify({
    identityToken: credential.identityToken,
    name: credential.fullName?.givenName,
  }),
});
```

